    "summary": "Electric The Other One/Cryptical suite plus tight China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The show shines with a blazing The Other One/Cryptical sandwich, a crisp China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider pair, and an inspired Bird Song. Jerry's Telecaster leads the high‑energy flow while Phil’s bass drives the improvisations. The Miller soundboard capture presents the performance in excellent detail.",
    "review": "August 23, 1971 at Chicago's Auditorium Theatre finds the Dead in a high‑octane groove that still feels fresh today. From the opening of Big Railroad Blues through a rollicking set one, the band rolls tight and confident, highlighted by Jerry’s Telecaster‑sliced leads on Me And Bobby McGee and an immaculate China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue. The second set launches into a daring cryptic journey: Bird Song segues into Cryptical Envelopment, then a marathon The Other One/Me And My Uncle/The Other One sandwich that builds into a thunderous climax before collapsing back into Cryptical and a soaring Wharf Rat. Phil’s bass pops off with mad‑man eighth‑note runs that drive the improvisations, while Bill Kreutzmann anchors the rhythmic shifts with steady power. Ron \"Pigpen\" McKernan adds his usual organ color beneath the jams, though it stays in the background to let the guitars and bass shine. The Miller soundboard recording captures every nuance—crisp highs on Jerry’s lead, deep lows on Phil’s low‑end, and a clean drum mix—making this one of the most compelling snapshots of the early‑’70s era.",
